{"ld": 1389, "paper": "HP911", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Create the Building Opportunity Through Out-of-school Time Program", "sponsor_id": "h-cloutier-kristen", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-larsen-daughtry-matthea", "s-libby-james", "h-moonen-matthew", "s-moore-marianne", "h-murphy-kelly", "s-rotundo-margaret", "h-shagoury-daniel", "h-stover-holly", "h-zager-samuel"], "committee_code": "AFA", "committee_name": "Appropriations and Financial Affairs", "summary": {"text": "This bill establishes the Building Opportunity Through Out-of-school Time Program within the Department of Health and Human Services as a competitive grant program to expand out-of-school programming opportunities for school-age youth by increasing or enhancing current programming, reducing barriers for access to out-of-school programming and creating new programming. It directs the department to issue by December 1, 2026 program grant awards to eligible community nonprofit organizations or libraries and monitor grantee performance and, no later than February 1, 2027 and annually thereafter, submit a report to the joint standing committee of the Legislature having jurisdiction over health and human services matters summarizing the operation of the program for the immediately preceding fiscal year. The bill appropriates $5,000,000 from 2106 the General Fund to the department for the 2026-27 fiscal year to carry out the requirements 2117 of the program.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0911&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2026-01-11", "governor_action": "Unsigned", "governor_action_date": "2026-01-11"}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1389)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0911&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-128)", "url": "https://legislatu